#NEXUS

[ pérez-pueyo2019a_fig7: Time-calibrated sauropod tree, 25 tips, most of them collapsed clades printed in capitals. Neosauropoda is a four-way polytomy (Jobaria, Haplocanthosaurus, Diplodocoidea, Macronaria): the four branches leave one vertical line. The drawing does not put nodes midway between their children, so nodes were read from the lines, not their positions. Random-sample case (seed 20261106). Topology transcribed from the figure and checked node by node; topology only. ]

BEGIN TAXA;
    DIMENSIONS NTAX=25;
    TAXLABELS
        PROSAUROPODA
        Isanosaurus
        Vulcanodon
        Barapasaurus
        CETIOSAURIDAE
        MAMENCHISAURIDAE
        Turiasaurus
        Losillasaurus
        Jobaria
        Haplocanthosaurus
        REBBACHISAURIDAE
        DICRAEOSAURIDAE
        Apatosaurus
        DIPLODOCINAE
        Camarasaurus
        Europasaurus
        Tehuelchesaurus
        Euhelopus
        Lusotitan
        Galvesaurus
        More_derived_brachiosaurids
        Sauroposeidon
        Phuwiangosaurus
        Tastavinsaurus
        TITANOSAURIA
    ;
END;

BEGIN TREES;
    TREE pérez-pueyo2019a_fig7 = [&R] (PROSAUROPODA,(Isanosaurus,(Vulcanodon,(Barapasaurus,(CETIOSAURIDAE,(MAMENCHISAURIDAE,((Turiasaurus,Losillasaurus),(Jobaria,Haplocanthosaurus,(REBBACHISAURIDAE,(DICRAEOSAURIDAE,(Apatosaurus,DIPLODOCINAE))),(Camarasaurus,(Europasaurus,(Tehuelchesaurus,(Euhelopus,(((Lusotitan,Galvesaurus),More_derived_brachiosaurids),(Sauroposeidon,(Phuwiangosaurus,(Tastavinsaurus,TITANOSAURIA))))))))))))))));
END;
